# AI Boilerplate — Aider Rules

Read `AGENTS.md` before writing any code. This file supplements it with Aider-specific reminders.

## Stack
- Frontend: Angular 21+ (standalone components, signals, zoneless)
- Backend: FastAPI Python 3.12+, SQLAlchemy 2.0 async, Alembic, PostgreSQL 17
- Auth: Keycloak (OIDC, JWT validation via PyJWT) — do NOT stub or bypass auth
- Contract: OpenAPI 3.1 (code-first — generated from FastAPI routers via `make generate`)
- Design System: `@aspect/design-system` — CSS tokens + CSS layers (no Tailwind)
- UI Components: `@aspect/ui` — generic building blocks only; app-specific components go in `features/`

## Non-negotiable rules — follow every time

ALWAYS read `AGENTS.md` (root + relevant subdirectory) before starting work.
ALWAYS scaffold features with `make new-feature name=<name> tier=<N>` — never create feature files manually.
ALWAYS define Pydantic models and FastAPI routers first, then run `make generate` to update the frontend client.
ALWAYS write a failing test BEFORE implementation (TDD).
NEVER exceed 350 lines per file (150 for Angular UI primitives in `packages/ui/`, 500 for test files).
NEVER use barrel exports. Use direct imports only.
NEVER use sync SQLAlchemy sessions. Always use AsyncSession.
NEVER use `any` in TypeScript. NEVER write untyped Python function signatures.
Every feature folder MUST have `manifest.yaml` with a `tier: 1|2|3` field.
Run `make validate` before finishing any task.

## Styling — CSS design system, NOT Tailwind

- Use design tokens: `var(--color-primary)`, `var(--spacing-md)`, etc.
- Add component styles to `packages/design-system/components.css`.
- Do NOT write CSS in Angular component `styles` arrays or `frontend/src/styles/`.
- Do NOT hardcode colors, spacing, or font sizes.
- UI component selectors use `ui-` prefix (e.g., `ui-button`, `ui-card`), NOT `app-`.

## Frontend — NEVER generate
- NgModules
- standalone: true (it is the default, just omit it)
- @Input() or @Output() decorators
- *ngIf, *ngFor, *ngSwitch
- ngClass or ngStyle
- @HostBinding or @HostListener
- Constructor injection
- BehaviorSubject for local state

## Frontend — ALWAYS generate
- input() and output() signal functions for component IO
- signal(), computed(), effect() for reactive state
- @if, @for, @switch (native control flow)
- inject() for dependency injection
- changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush on every component
- host: {} in @Component for host bindings

## Backend layer import order (strictly enforced)
router → service → repository → model/schema
Never import from a higher layer. See `AGENTS.md` for full details.

## When using gh CLI
Always pass `-R vanmarkic/AI-Boilerplate` explicitly.
